// Every function the package declares is a symbol of the LLVM-C library: the address of each is taken, so
// the program does not link unless LLVM exports it under the name the declaration spells (the C name
// is LLVM and then the name here). The addresses are collected, none is null and all are different.
// The count is the number of extern declarations: the 327 functions the compiler calls that LLVM exports
// (305 the headers declare and 22 checked casts; the compiler's other 5 uses are Cone functions here),
// 17 functions beyond what the compiler calls, and the 14 per-target initialisers.
// A release build may fold the addresses away; this is a debug-build check.

mod symbols;

import stdio use *;
import collections use *;
import llvmc;

